All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed in the three modules:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: added case-insensitive comparison using `.lower()` on both the required role and each user role.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: changed `and` to `or` so matching the owner grants access even without the admin role.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: replaced mutable default argument `{}` with `None` and created a new dict inside, preventing shared state across instances.
- `add`: changed from replacing the quantity to accumulating it (`self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`).
- `reserve`: changed `>=` to `>` so reserving exactly the available amount is allowed.
- `release`: added a guard to raise `ValueError` when releasing more than was reserved.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: lowercased alphanumeric characters as they were collected, and collapsed consecutive separators by skipping a hyphen when the previous character was already a hyphen.
- `truncate`: shortened the text slice by `len(suffix)` so the total result length respects `max_len`.
